# TDD Rules

- Write or update tests before writing production code.
- Confirm tests fail for the expected reason before implementing fixes.
- Implement the minimal change required to make tests pass.
- Refactor only while tests remain green.

# Test Quality

- Keep test names, docstrings, and comments in English.
- Cover happy path and at least one failure path for new behavior.
- Use deterministic fixtures; avoid network calls in unit tests.
- Prefer unit tests first, integration tests only when cross-boundary behavior matters.
